# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.
**Never commit `.env.local` to version control.**

```bash
# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Find these at: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/<your-project>/settings/api
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-public-key>

# ── PostHog Product Analytics ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Find this at: https://us.posthog.com/project/settings → Project API Key
# Leave unset or empty to disable PostHog entirely (safe for local dev).
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel Analytics and Speed Insights require NO environment variables.
# They activate automatically once the app is deployed on Vercel.
# For local dev, they are gracefully no-ops.
```
